1
00:00:04,440 --> 00:00:05,479
We just finished

2
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:07,119
our acting class exam.

3
00:00:07,120 --> 00:00:08,159
Next up, we're going to

4
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:09,559
get our bodies moving.

5
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:11,239
What we're playing today is

6
00:00:11,240 --> 00:00:12,639
the Flag-Pulling Tournament.

7
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:14,119
Before the official match starts,

8
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:16,239
we'll first have a warm-up match

9
00:00:16,240 --> 00:00:18,159
to get familiar with the feel and skills.

10
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:20,560
Here are the rules of the warm-up match.

11
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:21,600
First,

12
00:00:21,601 --> 00:00:23,519
the eight students will draw lots to split into two teams.

13
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:24,520
Each round, the two teams

14
00:00:24,521 --> 00:00:26,479
each send two students onto the field.

15
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:28,599
Each student wears two flags

16
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:31,439
in their team's color around their waist.

17
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:34,079
The two sides compete within the designated area.

18
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:35,199
The team that pulls off all

19
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:37,800
of the opponent's flags first wins the round.

20
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:40,520
You can start drawing lots now.

21
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:44,480
I got yellow.

22
00:00:47,120 --> 00:00:48,760
Black. Yellow.

23
00:00:50,040 --> 00:00:51,040
Here you come, Bro.

24
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:53,039
You drew one so fast.

25
00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:54,399
Bro is here.

26
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:55,680
I'll take green.

27
00:00:58,680 --> 00:00:59,680
Green, go over there.

28
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:05,599
Each team, discuss first

29
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:07,240
which two members will compete.

30
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:08,800
I want to give it a try,

31
00:01:08,801 --> 00:01:10,639
because I'm just the courage guy,

32
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:11,840
not the brains.

33
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:17,279
So I'll be brave first

34
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:18,519
and see how it goes.

35
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:19,520
I want to try too.

36
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:21,439
Then you two go up.

37
00:01:21,440 --> 00:01:22,440
You two go first.

38
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:23,240
Why do we go first?

39
00:01:23,241 --> 00:01:25,281
Because compared to us two, you two look... taller.

40
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:28,639
No, his hand is injured.

41
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:29,480
I only have one hand left.

42
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:30,400
Your hand is injured?

43
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:30,920
Yeah.

44
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:31,920
I can grab like this,

45
00:01:32,520 --> 00:01:33,040
Both are okay with me.

46
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:33,680
You two play rock-paper-scissors.

47
00:01:33,680 --> 00:01:34,400
Whoever wins goes on with me.

48
00:01:34,401 --> 00:01:36,280
Come on, rock-paper-scissors.

49
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:37,600
Rock-paper-scissors.

50
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:39,240
Rock-paper-scissors.

51
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:40,840
Okay, you're with me.

52
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:45,159
Three, two, one.

53
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:46,160
Start!

54
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:48,240
Come on, you've got this.

55
00:01:57,480 --> 00:01:59,120
They picked the 1v1 mode.

56
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:04,359
If you can't beat them, run.

57
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:05,360
Come on!

58
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:08,999
Though you are younger,

59
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,119
I'm not going easy on you.

60
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:12,599
The two of us can move side by side like this.

61
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:14,039
No, listen to me. Pull apart first, like this.

62
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:15,040
Just like them.

63
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:18,800
Careful!

64
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:20,080
Careful!

65
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:25,159
A sneak attack, he got...

66
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:26,520
Yeah, just like that.

67
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:31,719
It fell off.

68
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:33,679
Wait, you crossed the line.

69
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:34,320
Hold on.

70
00:02:34,321 --> 00:02:36,120
Wait a second.

71
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:44,760
No.

72
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:45,360
It's fine.

73
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:46,200
Why did you get 'killed'?

74
00:02:46,201 --> 00:02:47,639
Let's try again.

75
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:48,640
Come on, get him!

76
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:50,120
Mingyang, go!

77
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:01,800
Come on.

78
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:11,960
Mingyang, go!

79
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:15,400
You got this, 1v2!

80
00:03:24,160 --> 00:03:26,280
Congratulations to the Green team on winning.

81
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:30,880
Awesome!

82
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:33,439
Let's start the official match.

83
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:35,679
Director, do we have a trash-talk segment?

84
00:03:35,680 --> 00:03:36,160
Sure.

85
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:37,160
Trash talk!

86
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:39,880
Go ahead.

87
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,360
You're all doomed!

88
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:44,319
You scared us to death.

89
00:03:44,320 --> 00:03:45,399
You know why?

90
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:47,000
Because our momentum is unbeatable.

91
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:48,560
We're standing here right now.

92
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:49,320
We're like giants.

93
00:03:49,321 --> 00:03:51,159
And you're like little dwarfs.

94
00:03:51,160 --> 00:03:52,160
Alright.

95
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:53,360
Not much to say.

96
00:03:54,080 --> 00:03:55,040
But we're standing

97
00:03:55,041 --> 00:03:57,080
on your shoulders.

98
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:01,880
I don't even need to imagine beating you.

99
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:07,680
We're all the same age.

100
00:04:07,681 --> 00:04:09,280
I didn't mean to crush you.

101
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:14,679
I think there's no need to say so much.

102
00:04:14,680 --> 00:04:15,600
Just wait and see the results.

103
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:16,040
Okay.

104
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:16,440
Come on.

105
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:18,639
Now, the official game rules:

106
00:04:18,640 --> 00:04:20,719
We'll continue with the two-team showdown format.

107
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:23,079
4V4, everyone plays.

108
00:04:23,080 --> 00:04:25,399
Each team designates one member

109
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:26,559
as the captain

110
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:28,239
The first group to pull off

111
00:04:28,240 --> 00:04:30,399
the opposing captain's two flags

112
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:31,400
wins.

113
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:34,000
I think it's like this.

114
00:04:34,001 --> 00:04:35,079
They'll definitely choose

115
00:04:35,080 --> 00:04:37,239
that guy as captain.

116
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:38,799
I recommend you, kid.

117
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:39,879
Yes.

118
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:40,440
I recommend you too.

119
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:40,920
Right.

120
00:04:40,921 --> 00:04:42,079
Because they'll definitely think

121
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:43,399
we'll make you captain.

122
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:44,440
They'll come after you.

123
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:46,200
I think we're a bit too close.

124
00:04:46,201 --> 00:04:47,480
Move back a bit.

125
00:04:48,400 --> 00:04:49,839
They'll definitely think

126
00:04:49,840 --> 00:04:51,879
I'll be the captain.

127
00:04:51,880 --> 00:04:53,119
So don't make me captain.

128
00:04:53,120 --> 00:04:54,359
You guys pick anyone as captain.

129
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:55,599
We'll predict their prediction.

130
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:56,959
We pretend he's the captain.

131
00:04:56,960 --> 00:04:57,640
Right, pretend he's it.

132
00:04:57,640 --> 00:04:58,160
I'm the captain.

133
00:04:58,161 --> 00:04:59,199
I'll just keep hiding in the back.

134
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:00,599
Then you get them

135
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:01,600
to pick you as captain.

136
00:05:01,680 --> 00:05:02,640
Right, just pick you as captain.

137
00:05:02,641 --> 00:05:03,841
Right, you're less noticeable.

138
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:05,080
Right.

139
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:06,040
So we do this,

140
00:05:06,041 --> 00:05:08,919
We'll do our triangle.

141
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:09,320
Then,

142
00:05:09,321 --> 00:05:10,919
We walk around like this.

143
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:12,839
No, you stand at the very back.

144
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:13,360
I'll stand here.

145
00:05:13,361 --> 00:05:14,880
You guys surround them like this.

146
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:17,120
Come on, hold hands.

147
00:05:17,440 --> 00:05:18,520
Come on, hold hands.

148
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:24,520
You do it.

149
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:27,880
I'll go like this, I'll stand here.

150
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:34,880
The first round is about to start.

151
00:05:36,440 --> 00:05:38,200
I think their captain might be Chen Zhixuan.

152
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:40,039
Three.

153
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:41,079
Two.

154
00:05:41,080 --> 00:05:41,800
One.

155
00:05:41,801 --> 00:05:43,400
Game start!

156
00:05:52,360 --> 00:05:53,760
I can't get into the little corner.

157
00:05:55,520 --> 00:05:56,800
Watch out!

158
00:06:16,400 --> 00:06:17,400
This is intense.

159
00:06:35,640 --> 00:06:37,360
How did a wristband fall off?

160
00:06:45,880 --> 00:06:46,920
You two, pull apart.

161
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:04,560
Out!

162
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:05,960
Zhang Ziyu is eliminated.

163
00:07:08,360 --> 00:07:09,280
Pull it off him!

164
00:07:09,281 --> 00:07:10,560
He's definitely the captain.

165
00:07:24,160 --> 00:07:26,239
Game over.

166
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:27,879
Congratulations to the Yellow team on winning.

167
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:28,880
Okay.

168
00:07:28,881 --> 00:07:30,280
So who's your captain?

169
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:32,440
It's you?

170
00:07:32,441 --> 00:07:33,561
I always thought it was him.

171
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:38,359
Alright, let's talk this over.

172
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:39,440
Let's huddle here and talk.

173
00:07:40,280 --> 00:07:41,280
I feel like...

174
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:44,519
Actually, I think this time

175
00:07:44,520 --> 00:07:46,319
it's really Sun Mingyang.

176
00:07:46,320 --> 00:07:47,879
Who will you pick as captain next round?

177
00:07:47,880 --> 00:07:48,680
Who will you pick?

178
00:07:48,681 --> 00:07:50,279
Let's just say it directly. We pick him.

179
00:07:50,280 --> 00:07:51,480
Yes, we pick him as captain.

180
00:07:52,360 --> 00:07:53,360
Really?

181
00:07:54,720 --> 00:07:55,919
Because they actually just said

182
00:07:55,920 --> 00:07:56,720
you guys picked him.

183
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:57,680
He'll definitely make us think

184
00:07:57,680 --> 00:07:58,560
it's not him.

185
00:07:58,560 --> 00:07:59,560
But I think it's him.

186
00:08:02,280 --> 00:08:03,400
I think it's him.

187
00:08:03,840 --> 00:08:04,400
So how about this?

188
00:08:04,401 --> 00:08:05,799
You be the captain, and I'll go distract him.

189
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:06,440
Sure.

190
00:08:06,441 --> 00:08:08,399
So while we two are grabbing others,

191
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:09,439
Just try to keep him safe.

192
00:08:09,440 --> 00:08:10,880
Then you be the main rusher.

193
00:08:13,280 --> 00:08:14,519
Can you be the captain?

194
00:08:14,520 --> 00:08:15,120
Sure.

195
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:15,920
You're captain again?

196
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:16,560
Yeah.

197
00:08:16,561 --> 00:08:18,480
We just need to guess which one of them it is.

198
00:08:27,320 --> 00:08:29,680
The tallest one is the captain.

199
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:34,960
Once we pull off the tallest one's flags, I think we'll win.

200
00:08:35,800 --> 00:08:37,319
No matter who the captain is,

201
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:38,640
we pull anyway.

202
00:08:38,960 --> 00:08:39,840
Pull it!

203
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:40,960
Pull it!

204
00:08:41,120 --> 00:08:42,200
If you suck, practice more.

205
00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:04,120
No way.

206
00:09:04,121 --> 00:09:05,639
I already pulled off your flags.

207
00:09:05,640 --> 00:09:06,240
I've lost both of mine.

208
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:06,840
Right?

209
00:09:06,841 --> 00:09:08,520
Game over.

210
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:13,200
Congratulations to the Yellow team on winning.

211
00:09:50,560 --> 00:09:52,040
That was amazing.

212
00:09:55,280 --> 00:09:56,400
Come on.

213
00:09:59,680 --> 00:10:01,079
We figured you out.

214
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:02,960
What? What?

215
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:04,520
Too bad.

216
00:10:05,680 --> 00:10:07,000
Do we play three rounds, sir?

217
00:10:07,040 --> 00:10:07,760
Congratulations.

218
00:10:07,761 --> 00:10:08,799
We'll give you our

219
00:10:08,800 --> 00:10:10,160
Deluxe Toiletry Bag.

220
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:12,480
Where is it?

221
00:10:16,080 --> 00:10:18,680
You'll share your Deluxe Toiletry Bag in your dorm later.

222
00:10:18,840 --> 00:10:19,840
Okay.

223
00:10:20,400 --> 00:10:21,400
Back to the dorm.

224
00:10:35,920 --> 00:10:37,599
Since this is communal living

225
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:39,479
and dorm space is limited,

226
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:41,799
the show has decided to streamline everyone's luggage.

227
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:42,800
Next up is a

228
00:10:42,801 --> 00:10:44,559
Luggage Lightening Challenge.

229
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:46,479
Students will have twenty seconds

230
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:48,959
to rescue the items they want to bring into the dorm.

231
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:51,719
You can wear them, hang them, or whatever.

232
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:53,559
As long as it stays on your body and doesn't touch the ground,

233
00:10:53,560 --> 00:10:55,519
it counts as successfully carried.

234
00:10:55,520 --> 00:10:56,920
Twenty seconds.

235
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:01,439
Hanging on our bodies.

236
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:02,599
Does wearing it count?

237
00:11:02,600 --> 00:11:03,440
Yes.

238
00:11:03,441 --> 00:11:04,519
Anything in your mouth counts too.

239
00:11:04,520 --> 00:11:06,919
Is there anything that we absolutely need to survive?

240
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:07,600
What do we do?

241
00:11:07,601 --> 00:11:09,040
It's basically all clothes.

242
00:11:10,280 --> 00:11:13,439
So personal items have to be worn on the body.

243
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:15,599
What about personal items then?

244
00:11:15,600 --> 00:11:16,440
Since Bai Guanyu

245
00:11:16,441 --> 00:11:18,679
got first place in the first Placement Assessment,

246
00:11:18,680 --> 00:11:21,359
as a reward, he'll get double the time,

247
00:11:21,360 --> 00:11:22,680
which is forty seconds.

248
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:24,360
Well, thank you.

249
00:11:24,361 --> 00:11:25,999
Thank you.

250
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,359
Okay, then I'll go first.

251
00:11:27,360 --> 00:11:28,360
I'll go first.

252
00:11:34,760 --> 00:11:35,960
I'm a little nervous.

253
00:11:39,680 --> 00:11:41,240
He brought a gaming laptop.

254
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:43,200
Yes, this one's a must.

255
00:11:43,920 --> 00:11:44,480
Five.

256
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:45,120
Four.

257
00:11:45,120 --> 00:11:45,480
Three.

258
00:11:45,481 --> 00:11:46,519
That fast?

259
00:11:46,520 --> 00:11:47,679
Two.

260
00:11:47,680 --> 00:11:48,320
One.

261
00:11:48,320 --> 00:11:49,200
Time's up.

262
00:11:49,201 --> 00:11:51,719
Alright, that's it then.

263
00:11:51,720 --> 00:11:53,639
This is all I have.

264
00:11:53,640 --> 00:11:56,360
This is my big bag of snacks.

265
00:11:57,880 --> 00:11:59,359
What do I do with this?

266
00:11:59,360 --> 00:12:00,840
Just deal with it.

267
00:12:01,880 --> 00:12:02,999
The time was so short.

268
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:05,560
Even your double time wasn't really enough.

269
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:08,400
I'm totally lost.

270
00:12:08,920 --> 00:12:10,439
We'll hold onto it for now.

271
00:12:10,440 --> 00:12:11,440
Okay.

272
00:12:18,560 --> 00:12:19,920
Open this pocket first.

273
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:22,640
Right.

274
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:25,440
Their pants don't have pockets.

275
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:31,840
And unlock the code?

276
00:12:35,880 --> 00:12:38,440
Chen Zhixuan, fifteen seconds have already passed.

277
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:06,079
He keeps dropping items, Bro.

278
00:13:06,080 --> 00:13:07,000
And these are all

279
00:13:07,001 --> 00:13:08,639
some supplements I brought.

280
00:13:08,640 --> 00:13:10,079
You can all drink these.

281
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:11,759
Things you can mix with water.

282
00:13:11,760 --> 00:13:13,879
And I also randomly grabbed some clothes

283
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:15,800
and my comfort objects.

284
00:13:16,720 --> 00:13:17,839
Come on, let's lay it flat first.

285
00:13:17,840 --> 00:13:19,080
Hurry, let's lay it flat first.

286
00:13:25,920 --> 00:13:26,960
Three, two, one, go!

287
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:32,680
This one needs a code.

288
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:35,320
Another combination lock.

289
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:37,520
Oh no.

290
00:13:38,200 --> 00:13:39,319
Isn't this taking too long?

291
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:39,800
